  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Psychosocial support &amp; integrated livelihoods project (as part of the exit period activities)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hope and Homes for Children has been active in Rwanda since 2001 with a clear mission to enable children to experience family life and to achieve their full potentials. HHC&#x2019;s programme in Rwanda aims to develop sustainable community and family based care for orphan and vulnerable children, and to build the capacity of the local administration, professionals and communities to deliver adequate and timely services to vulnerable children. 

The current project will be implemented as part of CAFOD ID refocusing process. the activities that will be executed will help us to maintain the results that we already produced during the previous years and sustain the psychosocial support to children, mainly those headed household or those taking care of their brothers and little sisters.</narrative>
  </description>
